# Notice

## About ASD-STE100

ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English is a specification of ASD, the Aerospace, Security and
Defence Industries Association of Europe. The STE Maintenance Group maintains it. The current issue
is Issue 9, January 2025.

**This package is not the specification.** It is an independent work.

- The files in `references/` **paraphrase** the writing rules. They do not reproduce the text of the
  specification.
- The package does **not** contain Part 2, the dictionary of about 900 approved words. That
  dictionary is the core of the standard.
- `references/word-substitutions.md` is an illustrative list. It is not the dictionary, and it is
  not a substitute for the dictionary.

Therefore this package cannot prove that a text conforms to ASD-STE100. Neither can the checker
script. The skill instructs the agent to state this limit to the user.

ASD gives the specification to everyone free of charge, as a PDF. Request your copy at
`https://www.asd-ste100.org/`. Read the official document before you rely on any rule number in this
package.

`ASD-STE100` and `Simplified Technical English` are the property of their owners. This package
claims no affiliation with ASD and no endorsement by ASD.

